## 🔍 Bias Axes

This study examines three dimensions of hidden bias in LLM-assisted peer reviews:

### 🏛️ Affiliation / Prestige Bias

Evaluates whether LLMs treat reviewers differently based on institutional ranking and prestige.

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Config** | [configs/affiliations_ranked_stronger_vs_ranked_lower_global.json](configs/affiliations_ranked_stronger_vs_ranked_lower_global.json) |
| **Conditions** | `Ranked stronger` vs `Ranked lower` |
| **Additional Data** | [configs/author_affiliation_same_country.json](configs/author_affiliation_same_country.json) |

### 👨‍🎓 Seniority Bias

Tests whether review quality and tone differ based on author career stage and experience.

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Config** | [configs/about_author_profiles.json](configs/about_author_profiles.json) |
| **Conditions** | `Senior PI (20 years post-PhD)` vs `Undergraduate Student` |
| **Results** | [results/responses_grouped_about_author/](results/responses_grouped_about_author/) |

### 📈 Publication History Bias

Examines whether prior publication success influences how LLMs evaluate new work.

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Config** | [configs/publication_history.json](configs/publication_history.json) |
| **Conditions** | `100 top-tier publications` vs `0 top-tier publications` |
| **Results** | [results/responses_grouped_author_publication_history/](results/responses_grouped_author_publication_history/) |

---

## 📁 Repository Layout

```text
llm-review-bias/
├── configs/                    # 🔧 Experiment condition definitions
│   ├── affiliations_ranked_stronger_vs_ranked_lower_global.json
│   ├── about_author_profiles.json
│   ├── author_affiliation_same_country.json
│   └── publication_history.json
├── src/                        # 🔨 Prompting, inference, preprocessing utilities
├── results/                    # 💾 Released model outputs and grouped reviews
│   ├── responses_grouped_about_author/
│   └── responses_grouped_author_publication_history/
├── data/                       # 📊 Metadata and paper-ID index
│   ├── paper_ids_used.csv
│   └── iclr2025_metadata_by_id.json
├── visualization_code/         # 📈 Analysis scripts for released outputs
└── README.md
```
